 "_note": "The long-term memory end to end through coop_cli --serve (memory_tests.py). A scenario: its own memory file ('new'), the file of an earlier scenario ('reuse:<name>'), none, or a file of garbage; the brain's language, the chain (the decoder on the CPU), the reply tables and the habit; steps: a line said with the crosshair on a thing (by its key; the world's ids change on every line as the game's do), with the world's map changed, things left out or added; a serve command; a pause. 'expect': dotted paths into the reply ('turns.#' a count) and their values; {'starts': s}, {'contains': s}, {'not': v}, {'absent': true}, {'in': [...]}, {'has': v} (a list holds v). An entity id is read without its count. A scenario's 'tags' give its things tags by key ({'D_1': ['inside']}: a door whose inside the level marks, a room behind it).",
